INSERT INTO agreements (id, kind, version, title, body_sha256, body_text, attorney_reviewed, effective_at, created_at) VALUES
('agr_custom_development_agreement_2026_11_published_1', 'custom_development_agreement', '2026-11-published-1', 'Custom development agreement', '85501481b671d36e92a09aee60192a4bdc071add167b888dabdbe9f86ffa9362', '# Custom development agreement
The agreement that governs custom website and software projects quoted individually.

## Parties
This agreement is between Crestmont Website Development (legal entity to be confirmed) ("Crestmont") and the customer organisation named on the accepted quote ("you"). It applies to custom projects quoted individually, not to the fixed-price packages.

## Scope
The scope is the line items, deliverables and assumptions in the written quote you accept in the customer portal. The quote version you accepted is recorded with its date, the person who accepted it and a fingerprint of its text. Anything not in the accepted quote is out of scope.

## Payment schedule
- 50% of the quoted total is invoiced when you accept the quote; work is scheduled once it is paid.
- 25% is invoiced at the design-approval milestone.
- The final 25% is invoiced when the site is ready to launch; launch takes place once it is paid.
- Each milestone is invoiced once. Amounts are calculated by the platform from the accepted quote, never entered by hand.

## Change orders
Work outside the accepted scope needs a written change order stating the added scope, the price and any change to the timeline. Change-order work starts only after you approve it and, where the change order says so, after it is paid.

## Your responsibilities
- Provide content, brand assets, credentials and decisions needed for the work.
- Review and respond to approval requests and revision rounds.
- Confirm you have the rights to the materials you supply.

## Timeline and inactivity
Dates in the project plan assume timely responses. If we are waiting on you, reminders are sent after 7 and 14 days, the project is escalated after 21 days and may be paused after 30 days. A paused project can be restarted; it is never cancelled without notice.

## Acceptance and launch
Before launch the work passes Crestmont''s internal quality checks and is presented for your approval. Launch requires your recorded approval and payment of the final milestone. After launch you record final acceptance of the handoff.

## Ownership
When all amounts due under this agreement are paid, the custom work product created for you is assigned to you, except third-party components (themes, plugins, fonts, libraries, stock media and services), which stay under their own licences, and Crestmont''s pre-existing tools and know-how, which are licensed to you for use with the delivered work.

## Confidentiality and data
Each side keeps the other''s non-public information confidential. Where Crestmont processes personal data on your behalf, the data processing addendum applies.

## Warranty, liability and disputes
Crestmont will correct defects in delivered work that do not match the accepted scope when reported within the warranty period. The warranty period, any limitation of liability, the governing law and the dispute-resolution process will be set during attorney review and are not yet part of this draft.

## Termination
Either side may end the agreement in writing. Work completed and approved up to that point is invoiced at the milestone amounts already due; refunds are handled under the refund policy.
', 0, '2026-11-10T16:45:12.271Z', '2026-11-10T16:45:12.271Z'),
('agr_maintenance_agreement_2026_11_published_1', 'maintenance_agreement', '2026-11-published-1', 'Maintenance agreement', '82c456ea44b742b33d7fca491b01fc9f6eba0a7d8a1d545be4e308b21e0926b6', '# Maintenance agreement
The agreement for monthly maintenance plans.

## Parties and plans
This agreement is between Crestmont Website Development (legal entity to be confirmed) ("Crestmont") and the customer organisation that subscribes to a maintenance plan (Essential $99/month, Professional $199/month, Executive $299/month).

## What each plan includes
The services included in each plan (hosting, maintenance hours, content updates, security updates, monitoring, backups and support response targets) are listed on the plan page at the time you subscribe, and the version you subscribed to is recorded. Plan contents are awaiting final approval and will be published before maintenance plans are sold.

## Billing
Plans are billed monthly in advance through our payment provider and renew automatically until cancelled. Unused hours and updates do not carry over. Work beyond the plan needs your approval before it starts and is quoted or billed as stated on the plan page.

## Requests
Maintenance requests are made through the customer portal or a support ticket and are handled during staffed hours in line with the support policy.

## Cancellation
You can cancel from the billing section of the customer portal. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period. Your domain remains yours, and backups and handover materials are provided in line with the cancellation policy.

## Limits
Response targets are goals for an initial response, not guarantees of resolution time. Service levels, any credits, the limitation of liability and the governing law will be set during attorney review and are not yet part of this draft.
', 0, '2026-11-10T16:45:12.271Z', '2026-11-10T16:45:12.271Z'),
('agr_data_processing_addendum_2026_11_published_1', 'data_processing_addendum', '2026-11-published-1', 'Data processing addendum', '0486944cba00b7ff475efc7c50be72fcc5e7b79267be2c760ca46ae2e6a3fae2', '# Data processing addendum
How Crestmont handles personal data it processes on behalf of customers.

## Roles
When Crestmont builds, hosts or maintains a website for you, you decide what personal data the site collects and why; Crestmont Website Development (legal entity to be confirmed) processes that data on your behalf and only on your documented instructions. For data about you as our customer, our privacy policy applies instead.

## Processing details
- Purpose: building, hosting, maintaining and supporting your website and related services.
- Data: whatever your website''s visitors and customers submit (for example contact-form entries), plus account data of your staff who use the customer portal.
- Duration: the term of your project or maintenance plan, then return or deletion as described below.

## Crestmont''s commitments
- Process personal data only to provide the services and as you instruct.
- Keep it confidential and limit access to staff who need it, each with individual accounts, two-factor authentication and logged access.
- Protect it with security measures including encryption in transit, access controls, audit logging and backups.
- Help you respond to requests from people exercising their privacy rights.
- Notify you without undue delay after becoming aware of a personal data breach affecting your data.
- At the end of the services, return or delete your personal data unless law requires it to be kept.

## Subprocessors
Crestmont uses service providers for hosting, file storage, email delivery, payments and AI-assisted drafting. The current list of subprocessors and where they process data will be published with the final version of this addendum, and you will be told before a new subprocessor is added.
', 0, '2026-11-10T16:45:12.271Z', '2026-11-10T16:45:12.271Z'),
